---
title: Rios Vivos - Project Interaction & Security Risks
---
@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam defaultFontColor #000000
skinparam noteFontColor #ffffff
skinparam componentFontColor #000000
skinparam legendFontColor #ffffff
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #1f2937
  BorderColor #e5e7eb
}

legend right
|Severity|Meaning|
|<#7f1d1d>High|Prioritize mitigation; unacceptable exposure|
|<#92400e>Medium|Mitigate soon and monitor|
|<#1e3a8a>Low|Address as capacity allows|
endlegend

actor "Public User" as Public
actor "Admin/Editor" as Admin
actor "Monitoring Device" as Sensor

rectangle "web-page\n(Next.js - public site)" as Web {
  component "Public UI\n(browser SPA/SSR)" as WebUI
}

rectangle "system-admin\n(Next.js dashboard)" as AdminApp {
  component "Admin UI\n(content + user management)" as AdmUI
  component "Grafana Embed" as AdmGraf
}

rectangle "Edge Layer\n(Cloudflare/Nginx TLS + WAF/rate limit)" as Edge

rectangle "system-api\n(Sails.js on Docker/EC2)" as API {
  component "API Gateway & Routing\n(REST/CORS)" as APIGW
  component "Auth Service\n(login, JWT/session, reset)" as Auth
  component "CRUD: Home/Activities/Resources/Communities" as CRUDContent
  component "CRUD: Users & Roles" as CRUDUsers
  component "Monitoring Service\n(MQTT ingest, dashboards API)" as Mon
  component "File Upload Handler\n(media -> S3)" as Upload
  component "Logging / Site Config Service" as LogSvc
}

queue "Mosquitto (MQTT)" as MQTT
rectangle "Grafana\n(dashboards)" as Graf
cloud "S3 - Media & Uploads" as S3
folder "Logs / Site Configs" as LOGF
database "PostgreSQL (RDS)\nusers, reset_password, community,\ndonator, meditions, site_configs,\nlogs, monitoring_stations, etc." as DB
rectangle "CI/CD & Terraform state\n(GitHub Actions, tfstate)" as CI

Public --> WebUI
Admin --> AdmUI
Sensor --> MQTT

WebUI --> Edge : HTTPS
AdmUI --> Edge : HTTPS
Edge --> APIGW : HTTPS
AdmGraf --> Graf : HTTPS iframe

APIGW --> Auth
APIGW --> CRUDContent
APIGW --> CRUDUsers
APIGW --> Mon
APIGW --> Upload
APIGW --> LogSvc

Auth --> DB
CRUDContent --> DB
CRUDUsers --> DB
Mon --> DB
LogSvc --> DB
Upload --> S3
Mon --> MQTT : subscribe/publish
Graf --> DB : read metrics
MQTT --> Mon
LOGF --> DB
CI --> API : deploys/builds

note right of Web #7f1d1d
- High: XSS/CSRF and token leakage via browser; enforce CSP, CSRF tokens, secure cookies, and avoid exposing API keys in public env vars.
- Medium: Mixed-content and clickjacking risks; use HSTS and frame-ancestors.
- Medium: Dependency supply-chain drift; pin/scan Next.js deps.
end note

note right of AdminApp #92400e
- High: Privileged actions need strong auth; add MFA, session hardening, and short-lived tokens.
- High: RBAC gaps enable IDOR on admin APIs; verify ownership/role on every call.
- Medium: Grafana iframe could bypass SSO/CSP; restrict origins and enforce viewer-only service accounts.
end note

note right of Edge #92400e
- High: CORS or proxy misconfig can bypass auth; allowlist origins/headers and validate host headers.
- Medium: Missing rate limits/WAF enables brute force and scraping; tune per-route quotas.
end note

note right of APIGW #92400e
- High: Mass-assignment/IDOR across CRUD services; whitelist fields and enforce tenant scoping.
- Medium: Input validation gaps lead to injection and stored XSS in content; normalize and encode output.
- Medium: Broken session invalidation; rotate tokens on privilege change and logout.
end note

note right of Auth #7f1d1d
- High: Password/reset tokens reused or long-lived; issue one-time short-TTL tokens and audit use.
- High: Credential storage must be salted hashes; forbid default admin and alert on brute force.
- Medium: Refresh/session fixation; bind tokens to device/IP and use SameSite/Lax cookies when applicable.
end note

note right of Mon #92400e
- High: MQTT poisoning or spoofed stations; require TLS, client certs, and topic ACLs.
- Medium: Ingestion DoS via floods; rate-limit and queue sensor payloads.
end note

note right of Upload #92400e
- High: Unscanned uploads enable malware or path traversal; virus-scan, limit mime/types, and strip metadata.
- Medium: Public ACLs or long-lived pre-signed URLs leak media; default private and keep short TTLs.
end note

note right of DB #92400e
- High: SQL injection from CRUD paths; use parameterized queries/ORM validators.
- Medium: PII not partitioned; apply RBAC/row-level security and audit trails.
- Medium: Backups/replicas unencrypted; enforce at-rest encryption and key rotation.
end note

note right of CI #1e3a8a
- Medium: Leaked secrets in CI logs or Terraform state; encrypt tfstate, rotate CI tokens, and avoid writing secrets to stdout.
end note

@enduml
